.Dd August 16, 2026
.Dt HWTLM 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm hwtlm
.Nd hardware telemetry with OpenTelemetry output
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl -format Ar text | json
.Op Fl -per-core
.Nm
.Cm watch
.Op Fl -interval Ar seconds
.Op Fl -duration Ar seconds
.Op Fl -per-core
.Op Fl -format Ar text | json | otel
.Op Fl -endpoint Ar url
.Nm
.Cm exec
.Op Fl -format Ar text | json
.Op Fl -per-core
.Fl -
.Ar command Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
collects CPU power consumption (Intel RAPL), per-core temperatures,
frequencies, C-state residency, ACPI thermal zones, and GPU state,
and ships the results as text, JSONL, or OTLP/HTTP metrics to an
OpenTelemetry collector.
.Ss Subcommands
.Bl -tag -width "watch"
.It Cm list
Report CPU identity, RAPL power domains, temperatures, frequencies,
C-state support, ACPI thermal zones, and GPU state.
.It Cm watch
Sample telemetry at the given interval (default 1 second) until
interrupted or
.Fl -duration
elapses.
With
.Fl -format Cm otel ,
each sample interval becomes a set of OTLP gauge metrics POSTed to
the collector's
.Pa /v1/metrics
endpoint.
.It Cm exec
Read RAPL energy counters and temperatures before and after running
the given command, then report total energy, average power, and
temperature delta.
The child's exit status is propagated.
.El
.Sh HARDWARE SUPPORT
RAPL power data requires an Intel CPU and the
.Xr cpuctl 4
kernel module; temperatures require
.Xr coretemp 4
or a SoC-specific driver.
.Nm
degrades gracefully when either is missing: the sysctl-based
sensors (temperatures, frequencies, C-states via
.Xr acpi 4 ,
thermal zones) are architecture-independent and work on arm64 and
riscv given the appropriate platform drivers, while all power
columns are simply omitted.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The OTLP exporter honors
.Ev OTEL_SERVICE_NAME ,
.Ev OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES ,
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT ,
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS ,
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_COMPRESSION ,
and
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_TIMEOUT .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Sample every 2 seconds with per-core detail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hwtlm watch --per-core --interval 2
.Ed
.Pp
Ship metrics to an OpenTelemetry collector for 5 minutes:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hwtlm watch --format otel --endpoint http://collector:4318 \e
    --duration 300
.Ed
.Pp
Measure the energy cost of a build:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
hwtlm exec -- make -j20
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpi 4 ,
.Xr coretemp 4 ,
.Xr cpuctl 4 ,
.Xr bsdinstruments 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in the ObservableBSD project and was ported from
Swift to C for inclusion in the base system.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Kory Heard
